# Arcus button styles (mandatory)

Regardless of mockups or design refs, **always match existing Arcus control styles** — especially border radius. Reference: Payroll and shared `Button` usage (e.g. `/payroll` on [dev.arcus.co.zw](https://dev.arcus.co.zw/payroll)).

## Rules

- **Buttons are pills:** use `rounded-full` on all action buttons (primary, secondary, outline, ghost icon buttons).
- **Do not** use `rounded-md` / `rounded-lg` / `rounded-xl` on buttons for a “sharper design” look.
- Prefer shared `Button` from `@/components/ui/button` with `className="rounded-full …"` (and existing variants like `gradient-create`, `gradient-info`, `outline`).
- Typical primary CTA sizing in-app: `rounded-full h-10 px-6 shadow-sm` (or `h-9`/`h-8` for denser toolbars — still `rounded-full`).
- Filter chips / toolbar selects that look like buttons should also be `rounded-full`.
- Cards, tables, and panels may keep their own radii; this rule is about **buttons and button-like controls**.

## Examples

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — design-mock radius
<button className="h-9 rounded-md bg-[#2563eb] px-3 text-xs text-white">Save</button>

// ✅ GOOD — Arcus pill
<Button variant="gradient-info" className="rounded-full h-10 px-6 shadow-sm">Save</Button>

// ✅ GOOD — raw button still pill
<button type="button" className="h-9 rounded-full bg-[#2563eb] px-4 text-xs font-medium text-white">Save</button>
```

When wiring a new module from Figma/mockups, **restyle controls to Arcus** even if the mock shows square or lightly rounded buttons.
